Changes in this adaptation:
  RenderScript drawing replaced by GLSL; a small Qt input/model companion
  shares the same pulse state across Plasma's per-monitor renderers.
  The original 14-pixel cells/trails use Qt logical pixels on the desktop.
  Original pyramid detail and baked broad lighting come from the AOSP PNG.
  20 ambient pulses enter from random edges, change speed by +/-30%, and
  restart in a new direction/colour after their entire tail exits, with a
  random delay of up to two seconds. There is no fixed animation loop.
  A left-click release snaps to the grid and emits four different colours
  in the original directions at 300 pixels/second, using the original pool
  of 40 extra pulses. Existing bursts survive new clicks while slots last.
  Holding, dragging and right-clicking do not emit additional bursts.
  Android launcher icon-drop commands have no desktop equivalent here;
  the original tap interaction is mapped to left clicks.
  A fallback ambient preview remains available without the input companion.

Source comparison: Android 2.1_r2 and Android 2.2_r1 use the same pulse and
tap behaviour. Android 2.2 changed blend alpha to 0.8 and slightly adjusted
green/blue; this port uses that Android 2.2 palette and blend behaviour.

The companion sources are in package/NexusClassic/interaction/.
The small hooks for Shader Wallpaper's ShaderSystem.qml and ShaderApply.js
are in integration/ and are licensed GPL-3.0-or-later to match that host.
Shader Wallpaper is a separate project:
https://github.com/y4my4my4m/kde-shader-wallpaper

In Shader Wallpaper, choose this shader on both monitors and enable
Advanced > Experimental > Span all screens on each monitor.
Playback speed follows wall-clock time to keep independent renderers aligned.
